From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mangue OS <noreply@localhost>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 16:05:00 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] pwm: sun20i: report normal polarity for disabled channels

The ACT_STA reset value (0) made freshly exported channels default to
inversed polarity, inverting the duty cycle unless userspace set polarity.

---
--- a/drivers/pwm/pwm-sun20i.c	2026-10-10 16:01:34.918097241 +0400
+++ b/drivers/pwm/pwm-sun20i.c	2026-10-10 16:01:46.470120084 +0400
@@ -149,6 +149,15 @@
 	val = sun20i_pwm_readl(sun20i_chip, SUN20I_PWM_ENABLE);
 	state->enabled = (SUN20I_PWM_ENABLE_EN(pwm->hwpwm) & val) ? true : false;
 
+	/*
+	 * Mangue OS: ACT_STA resets to 0, which reads back as "inversed" on an
+	 * untouched channel, so a freshly exported channel silently produced
+	 * inverted duty cycles. Report NORMAL for disabled channels; apply()
+	 * writes ACT_STA explicitly when the channel is enabled.
+	 */
+	if (!state->enabled)
+		state->polarity = PWM_POLARITY_NORMAL;
+
 	val = sun20i_pwm_readl(sun20i_chip, SUN20I_PWM_PERIOD(pwm->hwpwm));
 	act_cycle = FIELD_GET(SUN20I_PWM_PERIOD_ACT_CYCLE, val);
 
